marble: apply AV masking inside SUSFS's compute_av copy

When BakaSU's selinux_hide feature is enabled, SUSFS installs
susfs_sel_write_access()/susfs_sel_write_context() in place of the upstream
selinuxfs handlers, and answers access queries through its own
susfs_security_compute_av_user() copy in ss/services.c. That copy never calls
security_compute_av_user(), so the masking added by 0032 does not run for
app_zygote carriers and detectors still read these edges as allowed:

  system_server -> system_server : process execmem
  untrusted_app -> ksu_file      : file    read
  untrusted_app -> lsposed_file  : file    read

Call the same masking helper from the SUSFS copy so both code paths answer
identically. The helper already limits itself to app uids and to the
root-manager / hook-framework types, so nothing outside those edges changes.

--- a/security/selinux/ss/services.c
+++ b/security/selinux/ss/services.c
@@ -3576,6 +3576,8 @@ void susfs_security_compute_av_user(struct selinux_state *state,
 	context_struct_compute_av(policydb, scontext, tcontext, tclass, avd,
 				  NULL);
 	susfs_spoof_avd_allowed_rcu(scontext->type, tcontext->type, tclass, &avd->allowed);
+	/* marble: answer the same masked verdict on the SUSFS path */
+	marble_mask_av_allowed(tcontext->type, tclass, &avd->allowed);
  out:
 	rcu_read_unlock();
 	return;
